  "body": "# Associated User Story\n\nAs an officer, I want to upload attendance for an event the same way I upload events, so that I can record who showed up in one step and members’ points and active status stay accurate without me entering each person by hand.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n\n**Officers can upload an attendance file and see each member credited for the event they attended.**\n\n- Sunny: An officer opens the attendance upload, picks a file (e.g., CSV) listing the event and the members who attended, and confirms. The system matches each row to an existing event and member, saves the attendance, and shows a success message with how many records were recorded. Those members’ total points, points by event type (service vs. personal development), and active status (7+ points) update to reflect the new attendance.\n\n- Rainy: The file is the wrong format, is missing required columns, or has rows that can’t be matched (unknown event, unknown member, or a duplicate entry). The officer sees a clear message with the row number and reason for each problem instead of a blank page or a silent failure. Valid rows can still be imported, nothing is counted twice, and a regular member who tries to access the upload is blocked (officers only).\n\n\n\n\nDefinition of Done -\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied:\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented;\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes);\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.\n(D) Deferred (Await feedback)\n- No inline \"Create Event\" if it doesn't exist which requires officer/manager to create one regularly before being able to import attendance.\n- Points uploaded are not distinct from points scanned at check-in.\n- Points are stamped with the import date, can be stamped with the event's date if needed.",
